course: dictionary
lesson: 8532
title: Saviour: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one. Saviour has three. Read the words around it to decide. «This umbrella was a saviour!» An umbrella is not a person, so here saviour means something that helps a lot just in time.
explain: When saviour means a person who rescues someone from danger or harm, the clues are often words like danger, rescue or trouble. Check by swapping in your meaning: the person who rescues someone from danger fits the sentence, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: With a capital S, the Saviour is a name Christians use for Jesus Christ. Look at the context. «All churches share belief in one God, Jesus as Saviour who died and rose, the Bible, prayer, baptism and love of neighbour.» Here Jesus is named as the Saviour, so this is a name, not an ordinary word.
fact: A saviour is a person who saves someone or something from danger or harm.
fact: The Saviour, with a capital S, is a name Christians use for Jesus Christ.
fact: Christians believe Jesus saves people from sin and death.
fact: Informally, a saviour can be something that helps a lot just in time, such as «This umbrella was a saviour!»
fact: US spelling is savior; UK spelling is saviour.
exercise: «The lifeguard was a saviour when the swimmer got into trouble in the sea.» What does saviour mean here? | A large boat with a loud horn | *A person who rescues someone from danger | A stone on the beach | A coat for swimming
exercise: It is a sudden rainy day and you have only a small bag, so a friend lends you an umbrella. You say, «This umbrella was a saviour!» What does saviour mean here? | A person who is very old | A shop that sells umbrellas | A loud sound in the rain | *Something that helps a lot just in time
exercise: In a Christmas carol you read, «a Saviour has been born to you». Why is Saviour written with a capital S? | *It is a name for Jesus Christ | It is the name of a town | It shows the word is being shouted | It is the start of a new sentence only
test: «The team had lost every game until Sam scored the winner in the last minute. He was the saviour of the team.» What does saviour mean here? | A person who makes the team lose | *Someone who helps the team at the last moment | A referee who stops the game | A new team kit
test: Which is the US spelling of saviour? | *savior | sayvior | savour | saveour
exam: In «Jesus as Saviour who died and rose», which meaning of saviour is used? | Something that helps just in time | *The Saviour, a name for Jesus Christ | A person who saves someone from danger, but not Jesus | A type of prayer
